<newsitem itemid="40892" id="root" date="1996-09-09" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Voltex lifts year shr, div.</title>
<headline>Voltex lifts year shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     21.52	 vs 18.30</p>
<p>Final div 4.50 cts making 7.25 vs 6.95</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   91.42	 vs 76.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   124.46	vs 105.63</p>
<p>    Tax			 34.70	 vs 30.84</p>
<p>    Net finance costs     19.41	 vs 18.34</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,509.22    vs 1,419.20</p>
<p>Full name: Voltex Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors have resolved to award capitalisation shares, in the ratio of 1.7 shares for every 100 held, to shareholders registered in the company's books on October 25.</p>
<p>Directors said the national electrification programme appeared to have fallen behind schedule but there were strong expectations of a new impetus in the current year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
